  "equipment_type": "Commercial boiler controller gateway",
  "applies_to": "Lochinvar Power Fin boilers in the 2.5-5.0 size range (the guide's \"Powerfin_2.5_5.0\" profile), read through the ProtoNode FPC-N54 gateway.",
  "summary": "Lochinvar's ProtoNode FPC-N54 start-up guide maps the larger Power Fin boilers (2.5-5.0) to 55 BACnet objects (Appendix C.7). Two BVs take the enable and tank demands, BIs give safety switch, flame, pump, valve and fan states, AIs give temperatures, firing rate, pump speed, status/blocking/lockout codes and the lockout codes of up to 7 cascade members, and eight AVs take the Modbus board command and BMS-supplied sensor values.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Appendix C.7 of the guide (pages 52-53).",
    "The table has no read/write column, units or states; access is inferred from the N2 type (DO/AO = writable).",
    "This is the ProtoNode numbering (objects 1-55). The Power-Fin list already in the library (lochinvar/power-fin) is the native Modbus/BACnet board map with different instance numbers."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Enable the boiler with BV 1 (Boiler Enable/Room Thermostat 1/Stg 1) and, for DHW, BV 2; send a rate or setpoint on AV 50. Read boiler 1 status, outlet temperature, firing rate, flame, alarm contacts and the lockout codes.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "Boiler Enable/Room Thermostat 1/Stg 1",
        "why": "Boiler enable / stage 1 demand from the BMS"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 2",
        "name": "Tank Thermostat Cmd",
        "why": "Tank (DHW) demand from the BMS"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 50",
        "name": "0-10 Volt Input/Rate Cmd/SP Cmd",
        "why": "Rate or setpoint command from the BMS"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 48",
        "name": "Configuration",
        "why": "Configuration register; see the Modbus manual"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 36",
        "name": "Boiler 1 Status Code",
        "why": "What boiler 1 is doing"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 31",
        "name": "Outlet Temperature 1",
        "why": "Boiler 1 outlet water temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 34",
        "name": "Firing Rate 1",
        "why": "Boiler 1 firing rate"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 8",
        "name": "Flame 1",
        "why": "Flame present on burner 1"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 14",
        "name": "Alarm Contacts 1",
        "why": "Alarm contacts closed"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 38",
        "name": "Boiler 1 Lockout Code",
        "why": "Boiler 1 lockout code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BV 1 Boiler Enable/Room Thermostat 1/Stg 1 and BV 2 Tank Thermostat Cmd are the demand commands; AV 48 Configuration, AV 49 Coils and AV 50 0-10 Volt Input/Rate Cmd/SP Cmd are the Modbus board command registers. The guide does not give the command sequence.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "AV 52-55 (tank, outdoor, system supply and return temperature) are writable so the BMS can supply those values; the guide does not say when they are used.",
    "setup": [
      "ProtoNode FPC-N54 to the boiler: Modbus RTU, 9600 baud, no parity, 8 data bits, 2 stop bits (IPW: 19200 baud, 1 stop bit).",
      "Give each unit a unique Node-ID (1-255). BACnet device instance = Node_Offset (default 50,000) + Node-ID.",
      "BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP is chosen in the ProtoNode web configurator."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Access is inferred: the table has no read/write column; BVs and AVs (N2 DO/AO) are treated as writable.",
      "The guide does not explain Configuration, Coils or the rate/setpoint command; they carry the Lochinvar Modbus board registers, so read the boiler's Lochinvar Modbus communication manual before writing them.",
      "Discrete Inputs words pack 16 binary states each.",
      "Lockout Error Leader / Member 1-7 give the lockout codes of the cascade members."
    ]
  },
